    "description": "Every Claude Code session starts with a fresh context window. Claude reads CLAUDE.md at the start of every session: a personal one in your home folder, a project one for the team, and CLAUDE.local.md just for you. Slash init drafts the first version from your codebase, slash memory opens the files, and slash context shows what loaded.",
    "companion_text": "More Claude workflows, step by step: follow Promptwerk. Based on the Claude Code docs (Memory, Commands), retrieved 2026-11-01. The editor and terminal are an animation, not a screen recording. Limits per the docs: CLAUDE.md files in subdirectories only load once Claude reads or edits files there; a CLAUDE.md is context for Claude, not an enforced rule.",
